validate/spectrum_ld_dev.log — running development log of the dynamic linkage disequilibrium of
the :spectrum closure (`spectrum = (; ld = :dynamic)`). Exploratory; everything here uses only the
diagnosis's discovery inputs (sets D and Dctl of validate/spectrum_diagnosis_inputs.csv) and their
kernel trajectories (the diagnosis's raw files, 10 runs per input, E6′'s seeds), unless stated.
Scratch analyses that are not in validate/spectrum_ld_dev.jl are described in enough detail to redo.

== 2026-11-14, step 0: the task and the starting point ==

The diagnosis (validate/spectrum_diagnosis.md) found the :spectrum emulator's k50 bias entirely in
V_G: (1) static, the missing negative LD at the move (~70% of the log k50 bias); (2) dynamic, the
genic variance falling too late under the move (~30%). The static `ldratio` prototype (P1) cancels
the two against each other.

Plan: carry the multilocus model's pair-class LD (src/multilocus.jl) alongside the spectrum's genic
variance: V_G = genic + D_t, D_t generated by Gaussian selection on the current V_G (Bulmer),
decaying at each class's split probability under CrossoverModel, carried through the move. Each
site's selection uses the regression of the genotype on the site, β = V_G/genic: directional term
β·aλ/S (the response is then V_G λ/S, as in the Gaussian lowering) and stabilising term
β²(a² + 2c)(1 − 2p)/(2S) (the rare-alleles closure's β² in src/multilocus.jl's hap_select, and the
multilocus genic loss (H/L)²/s).

Derivation of one generation of the LD of class c of pairs of distinct loci (genotype units, zygote
census; the multilocus recursion's T, R, Q with R reset by random mating): selection removes
ω_c V²/(4s) from each of T_c and R_c (in units of 2T), recombination T_c ← (1 − ρ_c)T_c + ρ_c R_c,
so without drift d_c' = (1 − ρ_c) d_c − ω_c V²/(2s) (Bulmer: ρ = ½ gives d' = d/2 − V²/(2s)).
Drift among n parents multiplies the expected within-population LD by (1 − 1/(2n)) (Hill and
Robertson 1968). One more term, from the non-Gaussian sites of the spectrum: under selection
without epistasis D_ij changes by Δln D = Δln(p_i q_i) + Δln(p_j q_j) (two-locus haploid
selection with multiplicative fitnesses: D' = D(1+s)(1+t)/w̄², checked by hand), so the LD of a
class scales by (1 + 2γ), γ the relative change of the genic variance by selection (the
variance-weighted mean of Δln pq over the sites), mean-field over effects.
At a fixed optimum without drift and with γ = 0, d_c = −ω_c V²/(2sρ_c), and with the genic
balance V²/(2Ls) = V_m (the β² stabilising term in the infinitesimal limit), the multilocus fixed
point gaussian_vg_loci: V_G does not depend on recombination, the genic variance exceeds it by
L V_m Σ ω_c/ρ_c (Lande 1975).

Mutations enter in linkage equilibrium (no LD), so D needs no term at mutation. Pairs of sites at
the same locus (class 1, ρ = 0) are not tracked: the spectrum's sites are separate (infinite
sites); two random sites share a locus with probability 1/L.

Expected generation over distinct sites: for a Poisson random field E[(Σv)² − Σv²] = (E Σv)²
exactly (Var Σv = E Σv²), so the generation over pairs of distinct sites is the square of the
expected genic variance (times β²): no correction for few segregating sites is needed.

== step 1: survey of the discovery inputs (scratch, survey.jl) ==

μ = 1e-4 per locus per gamete in every input (4Nμ = 0.4); α²/(2S) = 6e-7 to 2e-3; Σ_c ω_c/ρ_c =
17–33 at u = 3, 43–88 at u = 5 (under QTSim's lowest-point crossover, pairs toward the chromosome
end are rarely split, more so with more points).

== step 2: is the LD recursion right, given the kernel's own V_G, S and survivors? (scratch) ==

(a) Bulmer's balance at the kernel's pre-move V_G (generations −300…−10), S = ω² + V_P and
survivors n, d = −ω_c V²/(2S)/(1 − (1 − ρ_c)(1 − 1/(2n))) summed, against the kernel's LD
(V_G − genic): kernel/Bulmer median 0.723 (0.22–1.15) over D+Dctl+C+Cctl, lower at u = 5
(0.50–0.62) than at u = 3 (0.72–0.88). Fitting an extra decay x (ρ_c + x) to match gives
x ≈ 0.5–4e-3, unrelated to the site turnover 2κ̄ = 2·E_var[(a² + 2c)(1 − 2p)²/(2S)] (1e-6 to 5e-3
at the spectrum's equilibrium shape): with the turnover in a heterogeneous (by effect class) form
the ratio moves from 0.72 to ~0.8 only where α²/S is large (00854, 04095, 14872, 04943, 07602).
So site turnover by stabilising selection is not the main cause.

(b) Caveat on (a): the balance is evaluated at the kernel's V_G, which includes the LD itself.
The relevant comparison holds the GENIC variance at the kernel's and solves the fixed point of
the recursion (LD generated by the V_G it implies). Scratch positional.jl: per-locus LD
ℓ_i = Σ_j T_ij, H_i = t + ℓ_i (t the kernel's genic per locus and haplotype),
T_ij = −H_i H_j/(s(1 − (1 − ρ_ij)(1 − 1/(2n)))) with QTSim's exact ρ_ij = S(i) − S(j) for every
pair (S(c) = P(lowest point ≥ c), as pair_splits), solved by ℓ_i = −t A_i/(1 + A_i),
A_i = Σ_j H_j/(s·den_ij), damped; and the mean-field version (H_i all equal, the multilocus model).
(A first version of the mean field averaged the per-locus solutions, which is not the mean field
and made it look too good: kernel/mean-field ~0.95. Corrected; numbers below are the corrected.)

